venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# NOTE: this line alone does nothing on its own — data/posts.db was already
# committed to git before this entry existed, and .gitignore never affects
# files that are already tracked. It only actually stops being tracked
# after a one-time `git rm --cached data/posts.db` (see
# scripts/migrate_posts_db_to_jsonl.py's docstring). Once that's done, the
# durable record is data/posts.jsonl instead — see config.py /
# database.py's module docstring.
data/posts.db